- What metrics would you alert on for degraded tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Realistic API gateway policy is needed to manage multi-tenant CKNE dynamics at the edge. It tests your ability to translate CKNE signals into safe routing and concrete SLA guarantees, with observable metrics.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-driven token buckets per tenant
- Minute-wise rebalancing and fairness guarantees
- WASM/Envoy or Istio plugin implementation
- Telemetry for latency, throughput, and token usage

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple token bucket with CKNE scaling (conceptual)
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, burst) {
    this.rate = rate;
    this.burst = burst;
    this.tokens = burst;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  tick() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const dt = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.last = now;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.burst, this.tokens + dt * this.rate);
  }
  tryConsume(n = 1) {
    this.tick();
    if (this.tokens >= n) { this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test starvation scenarios and correctness under CKNE drift?
- How would you adapt the policy for multi-region deployments and clock skew?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design CKNE-aware real-time scheduling for multi-tenant streaming, focusing on dynamic backpressure, fairness, and latency SLAs.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-based rate shaping and budgets
- Token bucket backpressure per tenant
- Dynamic shard/windowing allocation
- Latency SLA preservation and telemetry

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal token bucket sketch
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.rate = rate;
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  consume(n=1){
    const now = Date.now();
    const delta = (now - this.last) * this.rate / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + delta);
    this.last = now;
    if(this.tokens >= n){ this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

